The attached image (Fig. 2) illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are retained at the injection site and cleared over time without systemic dispersion. Panel (a) shows whole-mouse fluorescence imaging of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11, indicating the adjuvant remains localized to the intramuscular injection site. Panel (b) confirms no accumulation in major internal organs after 21 days. Panel (c) quantifies the injection site fluorescence, showing a rapid decrease by day 1, a transient increase on day 2 (possibly due to edema absorbing fluorescent signals), and subsequent steady decline to approximately 20% of the original signal by day 21.